{
  "set": "kernel/public/v1/shuffle-draw",
  "kernelVersion": 1,
  "spec": "SuperEngine fairness kernel, kernelVersion 1: ShuffleDraw",
  "description": "ShuffleDraw(label, seed, j, t, m) = (u, ctr). Checks, in order: seed is 32 bytes (else seed-length); label is 1 to 32 bytes with no zero byte (else label-invalid); 1 <= m <= 2^64 - 1 (else m-out-of-range). Then limit = 2^256 - (2^256 mod m), and for ctr = 0, 1, 2, ...: x = uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(bytes32(label), seed, uint256(j), uint256(t), uint256(ctr)))), the hash of five 32-byte words in that order: the label's UTF-8 bytes zero-padded on the right, the seed, then j, t and ctr big-endian; keccak256 is Ethereum's Keccak-256, not NIST SHA3-256. The first x < limit gives u = x mod m and that ctr",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "vector": "kernel/public/v1/shuffle-draw/board-3-3-4-row-0",
      "description": "Cash or Crash row 0 of board [3, 3, 4], one loser, reference seed; j is 0-based",
